            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nIndeed, customizing built-in picker with CLI arguments is not supported. This is mostly to avoid extra documentation for which arguments area used by default plus the way to override them. The main CLI tool used in 'mini.pick' is `rg` which does have the global way to configure how it does the search.\r\n\r\n[Currently suggested approach](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/41487016b71506769c45afac1aee41a180e57fae/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1052-L1053) is to indeed either configure tool globally or use [`builtin.cli()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/41487016b71506769c45afac1aee41a180e57fae/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1143) directly with any set of arguments which will not conflict with the ones used by default.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
