            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski Sorry to resurrect this thread, but I have (hopefully) a quick follow-up question to this.   I am setting up mini.pick and ran into this exact situation with fd.   However I'm a bit new to lua and setting up my plugins (using lazy.nvim), so I'm not sure where to place the code snippet above (or if I need to tweak it first).  I have a **mini.lua** file where I import mini.pick like this:\n\n``` lua\n    { \n        'nvim-mini/mini.pick', \n        config = function()\n            require(\"mini.pick\").setup { }\n        end\n    },\n```\n\nDo I use this code snippet directly inside setup?  Do I need to use mini.builtin.files and set tool to fd?  Ultimately, my goal is to control the behavior of fd when picking files and eventually use this with my mini.starter config.\n\nbtw, using mini.nvim plugins has been a great experience and has made my journey into Neovim quite enjoyable so far!",
