            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Do I use this code snippet directly inside setup? Do I need to use mini.builtin.files and set tool to fd? Ultimately, my goal is to control the behavior of fd when picking files and eventually use this with my mini.starter config.\n\nPut any of the snippets from [this comment](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/830#issuecomment-2070194302) directly after `require('mini.pick').setup()`. This will create new `files_fd` picker which you can use like `:Pick files_fd`.\n\nYou can create a mapping for it with like this: `vim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>ff', '<Cmd>Pick files_fd<CR>')`.\n\n> btw, using mini.nvim plugins has been a great experience and has made my journey into Neovim quite enjoyable so far!\n\nThanks for kind words! 🙏 Hope you'll keep enjoying it.",
